Full mobile audit of the current app (iOS Safari + Android Chrome). Three groups:

iOS correctness
- viewport-fit=cover on the viewport meta: without it iOS resolves EVERY
  env(safe-area-inset-*) to 0, which silently disabled the app's existing
  safe-area CSS — and black-translucent PWA mode already draws under the
  notch. Header now pads past the notch; the draft roster tracker pads
  above the home indicator (whose reserved swipe strip was eating the
  drawer's drag gesture).
- dvh fallbacks where 100vh lied on iOS (URL bar): .main, .ktc-modal, and
  the rankings table wrap — whose max-height moves from an inline style
  into CSS so it CAN carry a fallback. touch-action:pan-x pan-y on the
  wrap lets the compositor arbitrate axes without a main-thread hop.
- 16px controls on coarse pointers: every text input/select was 11.5-13px,
  so the first tap into any field auto-zoomed the page (and iOS never
  zooms back out). Touch devices only; desktop keeps compact sizes.
- Popups (info/injury/VONA/pace/cliff) now position against visualViewport,
  so they stay reachable while the keyboard is up; overscroll containment
  added to the two scrollers the bounce-fix sweep missed (.ktc-modal,
  .tc-mgr-list); cancelable guard on the scheme drag preventDefault.

Touch-path performance
- The document-level scroll guard resolved the nearest scrollable ancestor
  with a getComputedStyle walk on EVERY touchmove (60-120Hz, every scroll
  in the app). Touch events dispatch to the touchstart element all
  gesture, so both walks now resolve once per gesture and are reused.
- Player-card sticky stat headers were bound once per SESSION while
  #pcardBody is rebuilt per card — they silently died after the first
  card opened. Now bound per element, refreshes coalesced to one rAF and
  measured reads batched ahead of writes.
- Popover closers (pace/cliff/radar) ran app-wide querySelectorAll on
  every tap and capture-phase scroll — now a boolean check until one opens.
- Team-header swipe primed BOTH neighbour previews on every touchstart
  (every tap); priming moved to the axis-lock instant and respects its
  cache. Tab swipe now pre-renders only the neighbour the finger is
  heading toward (reversal renders on demand).

Leaks, allocations, misc
- League Analyzer: laVorMap/laProjMap memoized on the build-list epoch +
  scoring/shape/lens signatures instead of rebuilt per render — a tab or
  chip tap stops paying ~1,100 object clones + ~4,500 regex calls before
  any HTML. Rosters tab logo tag was malformed (unclosed <img>) — fixed,
  and it plus depth-chart/roster/sidebar/share-row images now lazy-load.
- Player search: haystacks precomputed at index build (was ~12 regex
  passes x every player in the DB per keystroke) + 110ms input debounce.
- pushUndo: snapshots remember their serialization (the dedup re-stringify
  sat in the touch-down path of every slider grab) + a 160-snapshot
  global budget across teams (each snapshot deep-copies team state).
- Draft follow: the 2.5s Sleeper poll pauses while the tab is hidden and
  resumes with an immediate poll on return; --rt-h publishes without
  ResizeObserver too.
- contentRendered() checked innerHTML.trim().length — serializing the
  whole content DOM on every visibilitychange/app-switch; now
  childElementCount.
- Sharp league table: row/cell note-attribute split (like the rankings
  table) instead of duplicating context/source/team/relevance onto all
  ~384 cells per render.
- Bounded the weekly-stats and ESPN-gamelog fetch caches (oldest-first
  eviction via _tcCachePut).

Verified: 152 suites / 2257 assertions green (new test_mobile_hardening
covers the build-level iOS fixes, viewport helper, cache bounds, undo
budget, per-body sticky binding, pop guards, search index). Playwright
412x915: cards bind sticky headers on every open, search debounced with
correct results, sharp table renders with split attrs, no console errors.

